P('Explain why B can lie above the ideal reference at sufficiently high pressure and predict the effect of raising temperature and lowering pressure.',E('At high compression, finite particle volume is no longer negligible.'),E('The accessible space for motion is less than the container volume, contributing to positive deviation.'),E('Higher T and lower p generally reduce relative effects of attractions and particle volume, improving ideal behavior.')),
